{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1092", "sample_idx": 20, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e4b-it", "content": "## Lost (and Found) in Japan\n\nJapan. The word itself conjures images of ancient temples, bustling cityscapes, and serene gardens. My recent trip lived up to every expectation – and then some!\n\nI started in Tokyo, a whirlwind of neon lights, incredible food, and organized chaos. Shibuya Crossing was a must-see, and exploring the quirky shops of Harajuku was a delight. The sensory overload was exhilarating.\n\nFrom Tokyo, I took the Shinkansen (bullet train) to Kyoto. The contrast was striking. Here, I wandered through breathtaking bamboo forests, visited stunning golden pavilions, and participated in a traditional tea ceremony. The peaceful atmosphere was a welcome change of pace.\n\nFood was a highlight throughout the trip. From fresh sushi and ramen to delicate wagashi (Japanese sweets), every meal was an adventure. I even braved a vending machine for hot corn soup – surprisingly delicious!\n\nBeyond the iconic sights, it was the small moments that stood out: the impeccable politeness of the people, the meticulous attention to detail in everything, and the feeling of stepping into a different world.\n\nJapan is a country of contrasts, where ancient traditions coexist seamlessly with modern innovation. It’s a place that stays with you long after you’ve left. I can't wait to go back.\n\n\n\n", "logprobs": [{"token": "##", "logprob": -1.4305104514278355e-06}, {"token": "▁Lost", "logprob": -0.0012646066024899483}, {"token": "▁(", "logprob": -0.14694757759571075}, {"token": "and", "logprob": -9.536738616588991e-07}, {"token": "▁Found", "logprob": -0.0011703077470883727}, {"token": ")", "logprob": -0.14268243312835693}, {"token": "▁in", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "▁Japan", "logprob": -0.1014382541179657}, {"token": "\n\n", "logprob": -0.21057191491127014}, {"token": "Japan", "logprob": -0.5494483709335327}, {"token": ".", "logprob": -0.012566785328090191},